Functional Testing Learning Path
1. Testing Fundamentals
What is Software Testing?

SDLC and STLC

Verification vs Validation

QA vs QC

Manual Testing vs Automation Testing

Types of testing

Testing principles

Defect/bug life cycle

2. Functional Testing
Learn how to test whether an application behaves according to its requirements.

Requirement analysis

Test scenarios

Test cases

Test data

Positive and negative testing

Smoke testing

Sanity testing

Regression testing

Retesting

Integration testing

System testing

End-to-end testing

User Acceptance Testing (UAT)

3. Test Case Design Techniques
This is especially important for becoming good at functional testing.

Equivalence Partitioning

Boundary Value Analysis

Decision Table Testing

State Transition Testing

Use Case Testing

Error Guessing

Pairwise Testing

4. Defect Management
Learn how to identify, document, and track bugs.

What is a defect?

Severity vs Priority

Bug life cycle

Writing effective bug reports

Reproducing defects

Root-cause basics

Defect tracking

Tools to learn:

Jira

Azure DevOps

Bugzilla

5. API Functional Testing
Once you understand manual functional testing, learn API testing.

HTTP/HTTPS

GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE

Request and response

Status codes

Headers

JSON

Authentication

API assertions

Positive/negative API testing

Tool:

Postman

6. Database Testing
Learn basic SQL because testers frequently validate backend data.

SELECT

WHERE

ORDER BY

GROUP BY

JOINs

INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE

Data validation

Frontend vs database validation

7. Web Application Testing
Practice functional testing on real applications.

Test:

Login/logout

Registration

Search

Filters

Forms

Shopping cart

Payments

User roles/permissions

File upload/download

Error messages

Session management

8. Agile & Real-World Testing
Learn how testing works in development teams.

Agile methodology

Scrum

User stories

Acceptance criteria

Sprint testing

Daily stand-ups

Defect triage

Regression cycles

Definition of Done

9. Automation — After Manual Testing
Once your functional testing fundamentals are strong, move into automation.

A common path is:

Manual Testing → API Testing → SQL → Programming basics → Selenium/Playwright → Test Framework → CI/CD

You can learn:

Java/Python/JavaScript

Selenium or Playwright

TestNG/JUnit/PyTest

Page Object Model

Assertions

Test reports

Git

CI/CD

10. Practice Projects
Build your skills by testing applications such as:

E-commerce
→ Login → Search → Product → Cart → Checkout → Order

Banking
→ Login → Account → Transfer → Transaction history

Employee Management
→ Login → Add employee → Edit → Delete → Search → Reports

For each project, create:

Requirements → Test Scenarios → Test Cases → Test Data → Execute Tests → Report Bugs → Retest → Regression Testing → Test Summary

